757:
(a) All owners of body craft studios must obtain a permit from the director. No body craft shall be performed outside the confines of a current and validly permitted body craft studio. The owner shall apply to the director for a permit to operate in the county at least 30 days prior to the anticipated date of operation of the body craft studio.
(b) The permit application shall be on forms promulgated by the director and shall not be considered authorized or accepted unless and until complete in all respects, including the payment of any application fees. Application fees shall be set by the board of health.
(c) The application for a permit shall list the full legal names, home addresses, and telephone numbers of the owner of the body craft studio.
(d) Any individual or entity with any ownership interest in the body craft studio shall be fully disclosed, and the extent or amount of such ownership shall be provided to the director in the application for a permit.
(e) The application shall contain written proof that the studio complies with all applicable provisions of this Code, including, but not limited to, the county's building, gas, electrical, and plumbing codes and zoning ordinances.
(f) The application shall include the owner's written statement of policies and procedures that ensures that:
(1) No person under the age of 18 years shall perform body crafting upon any person;
(2) Body crafters shall not be under the influence of alcohol and/or drugs while performing body crafting procedures;
(3) No body crafting procedure shall be performed upon a person who reasonably appears to be under the influence of alcohol and/or drugs;
(4) No person under the age of 18 years shall be permitted to access any body craft studio;
(5) No animals of any kind shall be allowed in a body craft studio, except service animals used by persons with legally recognized disabilities;
(6) Each body crafter who will perform body crafting at the studio shall have a valid body crafter permit.
(g) The application for a body craft studio permit or for the renewal of a body craft studio permit shall be made on forms provided by the county board of health environmental health section. Such application shall be signed and verified by the owner.
(h) New studios.
(1) At least 30 days prior to the anticipated date of opening, the owner of a new body craft studio shall submit an application to the county board of health environmental health section for a permit to operate under these rules. No body craft studio shall be operated and no body craft performed without a permit that is currently under these rules.
(2) The application for a new body craft studio shall include:
a. A quarter inch per foot scale drawing of the body craft studio, signed by a registered engineer or architect. Such drawing shall show the accurate placement of each of the following:
1. Hand sinks.
2. Bathroom.
3. First-aid kits.
4. Waiting area.
5. Windows.
6. Doors.
7. Tables.
8. Chairs.
9. Room measurements.
10. Equipment.
b. A zoning certification obtained from the appropriate jurisdiction. The applicant shall comply with all applicable zoning, building, safety, fire, and other local codes and requirements;
c. A copy of the certificate of occupancy for the studio;
d. A complete description of all body craft services which will be provided in the body craft studio;
e. The full or legal name under which the body craft studio is conducted;
f. The address of the body craft studio; if the owner leases the location, the name and address of the landlord;
g. The name and home address of the owner; if the owner of the body craft studio is a partnership, the names and addresses of all partners; if the owner is a corporation, the date and place of incorporation and the name and address of its registered agent in the state; or if the owner is any type of association, the names and principals of the association;
h. A list containing the full names and home addresses of all the employees and staff who will be working in the body craft studio;
i. A copy of the written statement of policies and procedures of the body craft studio; and
j. An acknowledgement signed by the owner acknowledging that the owner has read and understands these rules.
(3) The applicant shall submit a non-refundable plan review fee determined as set by the county board of health and approved by the county board of commissioners.
(i) Existing studios.
(1) At least 30 days prior to the expiration of a body craft studio permit, the owner shall submit an application to the county board of health environmental health section for renewal of the body craft studio permit. No body craft studio shall be operated and no body crafting performed without a permit that is current under these rules.
(2) The application for the renewal of a body craft studio permit shall include:
a. A complete description of all body craft services that will be provided at the studio;
b. The full or legal name under which the body craft studio is operated;
c. The address of the body craft studio; if the location is leased, the current landlord and the landlord's current address;
d. The name and current home address of the owner; if the owner of a body craft studio is a partnership, the names and addresses of all current partners; if the owner is a corporation, the date and place of incorporation and the name and address of its registered agent in the state; or if the owner is any other type of association, the names of the current principals of the association;
e. An updated list containing the full names and home addresses of all of the current employees and staff who will be working in the body craft studio;
f. A copy of the written policies and procedures of the body craft studio; and
g. An acknowledgement signed by the owner acknowledging that the owner has read and understands these rules.
(j) Studios already in existence on the effective date of these rules and operating under a valid business license issued by the county shall submit an application in accordance with these rules for a body craft studio permit for existing facilities. The business license of any studio already in existence on the effective date of these rules may not be renewed unless all of the requirements of these rules are met.
(Ord. No. O-011706, § I(21-103(10)), 1-17-2006)

